what's going on everyone it is axl beats  here for anime uproar and today we have  another exciting entry into the jujutsu  kaizen manga with this chapter we have  officially entered the culling game and  i can't even begin to explain how  excited i am because i think this is  going to get wild very very fast if you  enjoy this video and you want to see  more jiu jitsu kaizen content on this  channel remember to leave a like as well  as a comment down below it only takes a  second but it is really helpful with the  youtube algorithm and of course if you  haven't subscribed to anime uproar make  this the video that you do so by  clicking that bell and selecting all  notifications you can also follow anime  uproar on twitter and instagram at anime  uproar or you can follow myself at  excellionyt of course this video will  contain jiu jitsu kaizen manga spoilers  as we are talking about the latest  developments in the manga so please  proceed with caution you have been  warned now before we get into it the  chapter previous was a little bit slow  so we skipped the week but i do want to  cover it briefly here chapter 159 was  called judgment and much like how 158  introduced us to hajime a little bit  this chapter 159 introduced us to hiromi  now hajime seemed to be a bit of a  cold-blooded killer but hiromi seems to  at least have some extent of a good  person within himself at the very least  he used to deeply value justice while at  the same time being disillusioned with  the law system in japan  hiromi was a criminal defense lawyer and  while i don't think that his backstory  will be super vital going forward we do  get a look at one of his cases where he  defended an innocent man at first he  actually won the case but upon it being  appealed the man ended up being found  guilty regardless he explained that he  can never really ignore things that he  believes to be wrong and when he  realizes that his client was found  guilty before the trial even started  again despite being innocent hiromi goes  on a rampage summoning a cursed spirit  as the chapter closes with a note that  the hammer of wrath was opened within  the courtroom so a few things to note  here firstly while hiromi is definitely  violent and dangerous as i mentioned  earlier his heart at least used to be in  the right place whether or not he will  continue to fight for justice is another  matter after realizing the corruption of  japan's legal system especially in a  post-culling game world honestly while  not much happened in this chapter it  really connected with me as well as the  town this story takes place in is  actually the one that i lived in when i  was in japan and while i was there i  always heard stories from people about  how i needed to be extra careful about  where i was and when not because the  city was particularly dangerous because  it absolutely wasn't however japan's  legal system has something like a 99  conviction rating the reason their crime  stats are always so low  is because whoever is suspected of a  crime tends to be found guilty of that  crime regardless of the reality of the  situation so i can definitely understand  being uncomfortable with that situation  pretty well but i can't even begin to  imagine how frustrating it would be for  a criminal defense lawyer who feels a  strong need to do the right thing  i can totally understand how someone in  that position might snap in the way that  hiromi does on to the current chapter  though that being chapter 160 entitled  colony we open up with a chilling image  of kenjaku the cursed spirit inhabiting  suguru ghetto's body looking down on a  woman and apologizing from within an  entirely dark realm the woman is  actually yugi's friend sasuke from the  occult club way back at the start of the  series and i kind of love that she's  back i don't particularly think that the  series was lacking for not having her in  it but i always did find it a little bit  weird that we were introduced to yuji's  friends only for them to vanish almost  immediately and never matter again  anyways kanjaku explains that he set up  a barrier around her area and that the  whole place will become a brutal  battleground in the near future  apparently he chose this area because it  was close to an old execution ground and  i'm kind of wondering if this was where  sukuna was killed or maybe even where  the original kenjaku was killed that  said the barrier seems to be very  difficult for him to put up so he can't  place conditions himself  anyone within the barrier will get one  chance to leave and i'm assuming that by  having this restriction the barrier will  actually be made much stronger than it  would be otherwise similar to how saying  a barrier is only working for gojo would  make it stronger against gojo  specifically i am more than sure that if  kenjaku had it his way he would have  wanted to keep all of the non-sorcerers  within it to die but it seems like he  can't quite do that so instead he simply  offers sasuke the opportunity to be  outside of the barrier when she wakes up  and obviously she chooses to get the  hell out of there but as kanjaku leads  her out of the dark dream realm we see  massive curses in the background and  what might be one of the most  interesting lines of the entire chapter  as he thanks her for getting along with  his son now if you remember from chapter  143 we saw that yuji's mom was also  inhabited by kenjaku this is crazy to me  like i am dying to see what this is all  about when did he take her over how does  being the child of a curse affect yuji  how is it affecting sukuna and finally  with this new edition of information  why does kenjaku still seem to care  about yuji at least enough to thank  sasuke for being his friend it is always  interesting when the big bad is a  protagonist's parent but i don't think  i've ever seen it where the big bad in  those situations is one that can  constantly switch bodies the closest  thing i can really think of is the 2003  version of fullmetal alchemist where  hohenheim sort of did the same thing but  he wasn't really the big bad in that  story he just kind of was very much tied  to the big bad either way makes for a  great plot point sasuke wakes up outside  of the barrier with the other member of  the occult club and it seems like  everyone here had the same experience  but the only one that kenjaku thanked  was her which understandably leaves her  pretty confused from here we cut to the  main group and they are looking for  angel in the list of players however she  doesn't seem to be using her real name  angel for those who don't remember is  the woman who's supposed to be able to  free gojo but the only hint that they  really have to go off is that she's in  colony too and they will know her when  they see her and that's not a whole lot  to work with however they really can't  just wait for things to sort themselves  out the time has come where they have to  join the game and the plan is that yuji  and megami will go to colony 1 while  panda and hikari will go to colony 2.  meanwhile kirana will stay on the  outskirts acting as communication akari  wants to go to colony 2 because that's  where hajime is supposed to be and the  strongest person should probably go deal  with the strongest opponent  i think yuji and hiromi should be able  to get along if they meet both of them  have a pretty strong sense of right and  wrong but i'm wondering if hiromi is  just a little bit too far gone at this  point to actually work with anyone on  the other hand with how quick to  violence hikari is and how itching  hajime is for a fight i don't think that  that's gonna go quite as smoothly as  they might hope  and yeah i'm sure that hikari is very  very strong but will he be able to deal  with a man literally in the process of  hunting down sukuna  i'm not sure about that one honestly  with that said though we finally see our  lads approaching the barriers and  officially declaring that they are going  to enter the colonies and with that  declaration of determination the chapter  comes to a close as the narrator says  that it is time to cross into the depths  of hades itself and the culling game  begins  this arc is going to be crazy i'm  expecting so many insane battles i have  so many massive questions that i need  the answers to like the issue of kenjoku  and yuji who this angel girl is and how  she will help gojo how our lads are  going to deal with the murderous hajime  and hiromi and now that sukhuna is in a  different colony what will ultimately  lead him into contact with hajime  so many huge things are coming this way  and i cannot wait but let me know your  own thoughts in the comments down below  like i said i am super stoked for this  arc but what do you think now that the  cullen game is starting what do you  think is going to happen and what do you  want to see happen  either way i'll be here covering the ark  entirely for you so be sure to subscribe  to anime uproar and ring that bell so  you don't miss any of our videos coming  your way and if you enjoyed this video  remember to leave a like and comment  down below to help us with the youtube  algorithm so we can keep making content  for you finally if you'd like you can  follow anime uproar over on twitter and  instagram at anime uproar or you can  follow myself at excellionyt i want to  give a big thank you to all of our  patrons over on patreon who allow videos  like this to be possible especially the  patron of legend the one who's  acknowledged by lord twego himself alpha  sigma as well are the one tier patrons  the ones who stand above all clans in  grata patahafa al-jatal hinokami and  water the toasted chi the spike 8227  corey mcgowan dylan isadore spidey life  tinnell tungsten tarcus baked buddhist  cody hebert and monkey d quilly finally  our pro hero tier patrons gilgamesh the  red-haired raven anel cruz rathwin de  ora very gucci alicia octor bonnie 